    <item>
      <title>Probabilistic multi-horizon spatiotemporal forecasting of injection-induced seismicity in geothermal systems</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04200-9</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Communications Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 24 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04200-9"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43247-026-04200-9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;QuakeCastNet forecasts seismicity rates and spatial distributions at two geothermal sites, where the network improves early forecasts, decay adaptation addresses shut-in conditions absent from network training, and the sites show contrasting temporal and spatial responses.</content:encoded>
